===Glyph origin===
{{Han etym}}
According to the version on bronzes, originally {{Han compound|止|王|c1=s|c2=p|t1=foot|ls=psc|nocap=y}}, hence the original version is {{zh-l|*㞷}}; see also the top component of [[出]] and [[岁]]. Later {{zh-l|*彳}} was added to form {{Han compound|彳|止|王|c1=s|c2=s|c3=p|t1=walk|t2=foot|ls=psc|nocap=y}}. Hence, the new character [[𢓸]] was coined.

Eventually, the right component was stylized into the unrelated {{zh-l|*主}}. The footprint pointing upwards on top became a point as in the character [[之]].

