====Usage notes====
{{also|w:Honorific speech in Japanese#Honorific prefixes}}
Primarily used or religious words, pertaining to gods or the emperor, as in {{ja-r|御%輿|み%こし|[[portable]] [[shrine]]}}. However, in this context it is often replaced by its homophone {{ja-r|神|み-|[[god]]}}, and a further {{ja-r|御|お-}} may be added, as in {{ja-r|御%神%輿|お%み%こし}}. The ''mi-'' prefix has also been merged into the readings of other kanji, such as {{ja-r|宮|みや|[[imperial]] [[palace]]}}.

